Usage: kast [options] <file>
  Options:
    --color <mode>
      Use colors in output. Default is on.
      Possible Values: [OFF, ON, EXTENDED]
    --debug
      Print debugging output messages and error stack traces
      Default: false
    --debug-parse
      Print extended diagnostic information and partial ASTs for parse errors.
      Default: false
    --debug-tokens
      Print a Markdown table of tokens matched by the scanner. Useful for 
      debugging parsing errors.
      Default: false
    --debug-warnings
      Print debugging output messages and error/warning stack traces
      Default: false
    --definition <path>, -d <path>
      Exact path to the kompiled directory.
    --expand-macros
      Also expand macros in the parsed string.
      Default: false
    --expression <expression>, -e <expression>
      An expression to parse passed on the command line. It is an error to 
      provide both this option and a file to parse.
    --gen-glr-parser
      Generate a Bison/Flex GLR parser for the specified module and sort.
      Default: false
    --gen-parser
      Generate a Bison/Flex parser for the specified module and sort.
      Default: false
    --help, -h
      Print this help message
    --help-hidden, -hh
      Print advanced options help message
    --input <mode>, -i <mode>
      How to read kast input in. <mode> is either 
      [program|kast|json|kore|rule]. 
      Default: PROGRAM
      Possible Values: [PROGRAM, JSON, KAST, KORE, RULE]
    --module <name>, -m <name>
      Parse text in the specified module. Defaults to the syntax module of the 
      definition. 
    --no-alpha-renaming
      Do not alpha rename anonymous variables in output.
      Default: false
    --no-sort-collections
      Do not sort collections before printing (for speed).
      Default: false
    --no-substitution-filtering
      Do not remove conjuncts of anonymous variables from substitution in 
      output. 
      Default: false
    --output <mode>, -o <mode>
      How to display krun results. <mode> is either 
      [pretty|program|kast|binary|json|kore|none]. 
      Default: KAST
      Possible Values: [PRETTY, PROGRAM, KAST, JSON, KORE, NONE]
    --output-file <file>
      Store output in the file instead of displaying it.
    --output-flatten <KLabels>
      (Assoc) KLabels to flatten into one list.
      Default: []
    --output-omit <KLabels>
      KLabels to omit from the output.
      Default: []
    --output-tokast <KLabels>
      KLabels to output as KAST tokens.
      Default: []
    --output-tokenize <KLabels>
      KLabels to tokenize underneath (reducing output size).
      Default: []
    --sort <sort>, -s <sort>
      The start sort for the default parser. The default is the sort of $PGM 
      from the configuration. A sort may also be specified with the 
      'KRUN_SORT' environment variable, in which case it is used if the option 
      is not specified on the command line.
    --steps <steps>
      Apply specified kompilation steps to the parsed term. Only for --input 
      rule. Use --steps help for a detailed description of available steps.
      Default: [anonVars]
    --temp-dir <path>
      Put temp files in this location. Default is /tmp/.<tool>-xxx
    --verbose, -v
      Print verbose output messages
      Default: false
    --version
      Print version information
      Default: false
    --warnings <level>, -w <level>
      Warning level. Values: [all|normal|none]
      Default: NORMAL
      Possible Values: [ALL, NORMAL, NONE]
    --warnings-to-errors, -w2e
      Convert warnings to errors.
      Default: false
    -W <warning>
      Enable specific warning categories. Values: [non-exhaustive-match|undeleted-temp-dir|missing-hook-java|missing-syntax-module|invalid-exit-code|deprecated-backend|invalid-config-var|future-error|unused-var|proof-lint|useless-rule|unresolved-function-symbol|malformed-markdown|invalidated-cache|unused-symbol|removed-anywhere]
      Default: []
    -Wno <warning>
      Disable specific warning categories.
      Default: []

